<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lingshou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lingshou was the capital of the state of Zhongshan from about 380 BCE until its conquest by Zhao in 296 BCE. Its remains lie near Pingshan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, where excavations since the 1970s have uncovered city walls, workshops and royal tombs, including the tomb of King Cuo with its celebrated bronzes. The name survives in present-day Lingshou County.</p></div>
